{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q3734518","formula":"Bi₄(SiO₄)₃","hill":"Bi4O12Si3","elements":["O","Si","Bi"],"composition":{"O":12.0,"Bi":4.0,"Si":3.0},"names":{"en":"Eulytine","ru":"Эйлитин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Eulytine (German: Eulytin from Ancient Greek: εΰλυτος, fusible, easily dissolved) or bismuth blende (obsolete) is one of the rarest minerals in nature. The composition is bismuth silicate with the calculation formula Bi4(SiO4)3 or Bi4Si3O12. The mineral forms isometric cubic crystals up to 2 mm in size, the supporting form of which is a tetrahedron or tristetrahedron.","ru":"Эвлити́н, иногда в написании эйлитин, ещё реже эулитин (нем. Eulytin от др.-греч. εΰλυτος, легкоплавкий, легко растворяющийся) или висмутовая обманка (устар.) — один из самых редких минералов в природе, по составу силикат висмута с идеальной формулой Bi4(SiO4)3 (или Bi4Si3O12)."},"fame":10,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-23331","atoms":82,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[10.268,0.0,0.0],[0.0,10.268,0.0],[0.0,0.0,10.268]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":2.567,"z":3.85,"el":"Si"},{"x":10.268,"y":2.567,"z":3.85,"el":"Si"},{"x":7.701,"y":8.984,"z":5.134,"el":"Si"},{"x":8.984,"y":5.134,"z":7.701,"el":"Si"},{"x":5.134,"y":2.567,"z":6.417,"el":"Si"},{"x":6.417,"y":5.134,"z":2.567,"el":"Si"},{"x":7.701,"y":1.283,"z":0.0,"el":"Si"},{"x":7.701,"y":1.283,"z":10.268,"el":"Si"},{"x":9.429,"y":4.295,"z":0.838,"el":"Bi"},{"x":5.972,"y":4.295,"z":9.429,"el":"Bi"},{"x":8.539,"y":1.728,"z":6.862,"el":"Bi"},{"x":8.539,"y":8.539,"z":8.539,"el":"Bi"},{"x":1.728,"y":3.405,"z":6.862,"el":"Bi"},{"x":4.295,"y":0.838,"z":9.429,"el":"Bi"},{"x":1.728,"y":6.862,"z":8.539,"el":"Bi"},{"x":0.838,"y":0.838,"z":0.838,"el":"Bi"},{"x":